Subject: [PATCH 19/67] =?UTF-8?q?fix(aligram):=20D-07=20=E2=80=94=20anchor?=
 =?UTF-8?q?-loss=20ref=20drops=20release=20their=20deferred=20deletes?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Verified: dropRefAndDecrement, terminateLiveForDelete, onDialogDeleted,
onDialogClearedExcept and onChannelHistoryCleared never called
releaseDeferredDeletesForRef — only the startup sweep did — so a file
Telegram asked to delete stayed cached until the next restart. The
sibling D-06 fix already added per-ref releases in the four dialog
flows, but terminateLiveForDelete (ANCHOR_LOST drops from the delete
event / mark-path sweep) bypasses the funnel entirely. Fix: call
releaseDeferredDeletesForRef at the end of dropRefAndDecrement (the
single funnel) AND in terminateLiveForDelete (which inlines its own
delete). Idempotency verified: release only selects PENDING rows for
the ref (getPendingForRef) and marks them DONE after handling, so the
dialog flows' existing explicit calls after dropRefAndDecrement now
find nothing PENDING and no-op — no double release, no double file
delete. The release re-checks active pins per path, so a file another
ref still pins survives.
---
 .../ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java  | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java
index 6a4025059..dad57651d 100644
--- a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java
+++ b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java
@@ -2288,6 +2288,14 @@ public final class AliGramPreservation {
             dao.deleteRefById(live.refId);
             mirrorRemoveForRef(live);
             forgetResolvedFilesForRef(live);
+            // Phase 3.1 (D-07): this path inlines its own delete instead
+            // of going through dropRefAndDecrement, so it needs the
+            // release explicitly — otherwise a LIVE job dropped
+            // ANCHOR_LOST (delete-event with the delete axis off, or the
+            // mark-path sweep) leaves its deferred deletes for the
+            // startup sweep only. Same idempotency as the funnel: only
+            // PENDING rows for this ref, active pins re-checked.
+            releaseDeferredDeletesForRef(account, live.refId);
             FileLog.d(TAG + ": LIVE ref dropped ANCHOR_LOST for message " + messageId + " in " + dialogId);
             sweepRefcountZeroBlobs(account);
         } catch (Throwable e) {
@@ -2356,6 +2364,19 @@ public final class AliGramPreservation {
             dao.deleteRefById(ref.refId);
             mirrorRemoveForRef(ref);
             forgetResolvedFilesForRef(ref);
+            // Phase 3.1 (D-07): the single funnel for all anchor-loss
+            // drops — ending the pin releases this ref's deferred
+            // deletes now instead of leaving them for the startup sweep.
+            // Idempotent with the per-ref releases the four dialog flows
+            // (onDialogDeleted / onDialogClearedExcept /
+            // onChannelHistoryCleared / clearPreservedForDialog) already
+            // do after calling here: those find the rows DONE and no-op
+            // (release only touches PENDING rows, and the release
+            // re-checks active pins per path, so a file another ref
+            // still pins survives). Verified: the sibling D-06 fix added
+            // those per-ref releases; this funnel call makes the release
+            // happen for every drop path, including future callers.
+            releaseDeferredDeletesForRef(ref.accountId, ref.refId);
         } catch (Throwable e) {
             FileLog.e(TAG + ": dropRefAndDecrement failed", e);
         }
